/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  packing05_schulz_record_0p10bar  --  THE PACKING AS A RECORD: the bed of
  packing01_schulz_0p10bar, with its geometry read from a packing record
  instead of typed inline (DEV.md 4c C329 "where a packing's data live";
  C398 slice (e); Theory Guide sec:packing-record).

  WHAT THIS CASE SHOWS.  Three sources for the four numbers Rocha, Bravo &
  Fair read, each printed in the run with where it came from:
    * NOMINAL, from the record constant/assets/MontzA3-500M.dat: the
      corrugation angle (60 deg) and the surface (gauze), and the nominal
      area 500 m2/m3 -- all three as Schulz et al. print them (Chem. Eng.
      Trans. 69 (2018) 763, section 2, p. 764).  The record is CASE-LOCAL:
      no source in hand gives this packing's full geometry, so it is not in
      the catalogue.
    * INSTALLED, measured on THIS bed and declared by the case under
      `installed {}`: the area 478 m2/m3 "based on measured corrugation
      dimensions of delivered packing" and the void fraction of the dry
      packed bed, about 0.92 (same section).  The run prints that 478
      replaces the record's nominal 500.
    * BORROWED, a hypothesis of this case: the corrugation side, which
      Schulz do not print.  It is taken from the catalogue record SulzerBX
      (S = 9 mm, Rocha, Bravo & Fair 1993 Table IV), the gauze packing of
      the same area class -- the same estimate packing01 types inline, now
      named as another packing's value.  The seal (bin/choupo-import)
      mirrors that record into constant/assets/ with its hash, so the case
      runs with the catalogue hidden.
  Everything else (column, boil-up sweep, reboiler liquid, the liquid
  viscosity of Schulz Table 1, the property system) is packing01's,
  unchanged.

  THE CHECK.  The resolved geometry is the same four doubles packing01
  types, so every number is packing01's: `expected` is packing01's golden,
  row for row, plus three rows packing01 cannot have -- the geometry the
  record-backed bed was solved with, published as packing_specificArea_m2_m3,
  packing_voidFraction and packing_corrugationAngle_deg (478, 0.92, 60) so
  that a reader of the result, and the GUI's column sheet, see it.  The
  gate bin/curate/check_packing_record.py holds the two runs' KPIs equal
  exactly.  The same gate removes the `borrowed` block
  and requires the refusal that names `corrugationSide` and
  `RochaBravoFair` -- the field the correlation reads and the record lacks.

  MEASURED, ESTIMATED, FITTED: as packing01_schulz_0p10bar's header (the
  corrugation side is the one estimated geometric number; nothing fitted;
  every point of Schulz Fig. 2b at 0.10 bar held out).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        column;
        type        distillationColumn;
        model       totalReflux;

        operation
        {
            P              0.10 bar;      // TOP pressure
            condenser      { type total; }

            totalReflux
            {
                fFactor        1.5;      // swept; (m/s)(kg/m3)^0.5, reboiler vapour on the tower area
                specifiedAt    reboiler;
                composition
                {
                    pXylene    0.2;
                    oXylene    0.80;
                }
            }

            packing
            {
                record            MontzA3-500M;   // constant/assets/MontzA3-500M.dat (nominal)
                model             RochaBravoFair;
                diameter          1.22 m;      // Schulz section 2
                height            2.2 m;       // Schulz section 2
                installed
                {
                    specificArea  478;         // m2/m3
                    voidFraction  0.92;
                    source        "Schulz, Rietfort, Jansen & Olujic, Chem. Eng. Trans. 69 (2018) 763, section 2, p. 764: installed area from the measured corrugation dimensions of the delivered packing; void fraction of the dry packed bed, around 0.92";
                }
                borrowed
                {
                    corrugationSide
                    {
                        from      SulzerBX;
                        reason    "not printed by Schulz et al.; Sulzer BX is the gauze packing of the same area class (492 m2/m3, 60 deg) in Rocha-Bravo-Fair 1993 Table IV, and HETP is roughly proportional to S";
                    }
                }
                lightKey          pXylene;
                liquidViscosity   3.91e-4;       // Pa s, Schulz Table 1
                segments          100;
            }
        }
    }
);
